Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 06:56:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let a spec depend on the Sale/Rent pick, not just on another
 spec

"Pets allowed" belongs on a rental and means nothing on a sale -- a
distinction property_type cannot express, because it is the listing's own
condition field that decides it, not a sibling attribute.

resolveVisibleAttrs now accepts the listing's condition and treats one
reserved dependsOnSlug, '$condition', as referring to it. The prefix
cannot collide with a real attribute slug, which are plain identifiers.
Both listing flows pass their condition through; the parameter is
optional, so a caller without one hides every condition-dependent
attribute, which is the safe direction -- a hidden attribute is never
required and never saved.

The Properties specs that use this (and the eight new property_type-scoped
ones alongside them: elevator, maid's room, land area, balcony area, view,
backup power, water supply, year built) are already inserted live. The
pets_allowed row was simply hidden until this shipped, since no attribute
value is ever stored under '$condition'.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
